          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "If $x \\sin ^{3} \\theta+y \\cos ^{3} \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$ and\r\n\r\n$x \\sin \\theta=y \\cos \\theta,$ then $x^{2}+y^{2}=$",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "gKf84",
              "text": "1",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "wCaVg",
              "text": "2",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "QVfF7",
              "text": "0",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "6BK26",
              "text": "None of these",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "$x \\sin ^{3} \\theta+y \\cos ^{3} \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\nand $x \\sin \\theta=y \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\nEquation (i) may be written as $x \\sin \\theta \\cdot \\sin ^{2} \\theta+y \\cos ^{3} \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y \\cos \\theta \\sin ^{2} \\theta+y \\cos ^{3} \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y \\cos \\theta\\left(\\sin ^{2} \\theta+\\cos ^{2} \\theta\\right)=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow y \\cos \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cos \\theta \\therefore y=\\sin \\theta \\quad \\ldots$\r\n\r\nPutting the value of y from\r\n\r\n(iii) in (ii), we get $\\mathrm{x} \\sin \\theta=\\sin \\theta \\cdot \\cos \\theta \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{x}=\\cos \\theta \\quad \\ldots$ (iv)\r\n\r\nSquaring (iii) and (iv) and adding, we get $\\mathrm{x}^{2}+\\mathrm{y}^{2}=\\cos ^{2} \\theta+\\sin ^{2} \\theta=1$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
