          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 3,
          "question": {
            "text": "An object is obseved from the points $A, B$ and C lying in a horizontal straight line which passes directly underneath the object. The angular elevation at $\\mathrm{B}$ is twice that at $\\mathrm{A}$ and at $\\mathrm{C}$ three times that at $\\mathrm{A} .$ It $\\mathrm{AB}=a, \\mathrm{BC}=b$, then the height of the object is",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "jRlLS",
              "text": "$\\frac{b}{2 a} \\sqrt{(a+b)(3 b-a)}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "h9zt5",
              "text": "$\\frac{a}{b} \\sqrt{(a+b)(3 b-a)}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "cgM78",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{a}}{2 \\mathrm{~b}} \\sqrt{(\\mathrm{a}+\\mathrm{b})(3 \\mathrm{~b}-\\mathrm{a})}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "LTkVT",
              "text": "$\\frac{2 a}{b} \\sqrt{(a+b)(3 b-a)}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/rwdKoQrfKyk9Z0EX5JJEz95pGwrs8huU3BDOAEBcdXk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nLet $\\mathrm{ED}=h, \\angle \\mathrm{EAB}=\\alpha$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\angle \\mathrm{EBD}=2 \\alpha, \\angle \\mathrm{ECD}=3 \\alpha$\r\n\r\nNow, $\\angle \\mathrm{DBE}=\\angle \\mathrm{EAB}+\\angle \\mathrm{BEA}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 \\alpha=\\alpha+\\angle \\mathrm{BEA}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\angle \\mathrm{BEA}=\\alpha=\\angle \\mathrm{EAB}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\mathrm{AB}=\\mathrm{EB}=a$\r\n\r\nSimilarly, $\\angle \\mathrm{EBC}=\\alpha$ $\\operatorname{In} \\Delta \\mathrm{EBC}, \\frac{\\mathrm{BC}}{\\sin \\alpha}=\\frac{\\mathrm{EB}}{\\sin \\left(180^{\\circ}-3 \\alpha\\right)}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{b}{\\sin \\alpha}=\\frac{a}{\\sin 3 \\alpha} \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{\\sin 3 \\alpha}{\\sin 3 \\alpha}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{3 \\sin \\alpha-4 \\sin ^{3} \\alpha}{\\sin \\alpha}=3-4 \\sin ^{2} \\alpha$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 4 \\sin ^{2} \\alpha=3-\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{3 b-a}{b}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin \\alpha=\\sqrt{\\frac{3 b-a}{4 b}}$\r\n\r\nIn $\\Delta \\mathrm{EBD}, \\sin 2 \\alpha=\\frac{E D}{E B}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\mathrm{ED}=\\mathrm{a} \\cdot 2 \\sin \\alpha \\cdot \\cos \\alpha$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow h=2 a \\sqrt{\\frac{3 b-a}{4 b}}, \\sqrt{1-\\frac{3 b-a}{4 b}}$\r\n\r\n$=2 a \\sqrt{\\frac{3 b-a}{4 b}} \\sqrt{\\frac{b-a}{4 b}}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{a}{2 b} \\sqrt{(a+b)(3 b-a)}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
