    {
      "index": 4,
      "topicId": "64c0e86b6f5bfc7ab78aedfc",
      "title": "Transformation Formulas",
      "totalQuestions": 1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "_id": "64c0e7df6f5bfc7ab78ae89a",
          "previousYearPapers": [
            {
              "_id": "61a8bf0fc821b6514e527d7a",
              "examId": "615d7713c52ffa3c944600e3",
              "heldOn": "2016-04-30T09:00:00.000Z",
              "isVisible": true,
              "shortName": "2016",
              "title": "BITSAT 2016"
            }
          ],
          "type": "singleCorrect",
          "level": 2,
          "question": {
            "text": "If $A$ and $B$ are positive acute angles satisfying $3 \\cos ^{2} A+2 \\cos ^{2} B=4$ and $\\frac{3 \\sin A}{\\sin B}=\\frac{2 \\cos B}{\\cos A}$\r\n\r\nThen the value of $\\mathrm{A}+2 \\mathrm{~B}$ is equal to :",
            "image": null
          },
          "options": [
            {
              "id": "p6ctA",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "BD00l",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
              "isCorrect": true,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "1oSwK",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            },
            {
              "id": "bEZ2y",
              "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "Given, $3 \\cos ^{2} \\mathrm{~A}+2 \\cos ^{2} \\mathrm{~B}=4$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 2 \\cos ^{2} \\mathrm{~B}-1=4-3 \\cos ^{2} \\mathrm{~A}-1$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\cos 2 \\mathrm{~B}=3\\left(1-\\cos ^{2} \\mathrm{~A}\\right)=3 \\sin ^{2} \\mathrm{~A} \\ldots(1)$\r\n\r\nand $2 \\cos \\mathrm{B} \\sin \\mathrm{B}=3 \\sin \\mathrm{A} \\cos \\mathrm{A}$\r\n\r\n$\\sin 2 \\mathrm{~B}=3 \\sin \\mathrm{A} \\cos \\mathrm{A}$\r\n\r\nNow, $\\cos (\\mathrm{A}+2 \\mathrm{~B})=\\cos \\mathrm{A} \\cos 2 \\mathrm{~B}-\\sin \\mathrm{A}$\r\n\r\n$\\sin 2 \\mathrm{~B}$\r\n\r\n$=\\cos A\\left(3 \\sin ^{2} A\\right)-\\sin A(3 \\sin A \\cos A)=0$\r\n\r\n[using eqs. (1) and (2)] $\\Rightarrow A+2 B=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
            "image": null
          },
          "videoSolution": null,
          "questionLabels": [],
          "syllabusCategory": "noChange",
