            {
              "id": "ZwzQ6",
              "text": "$\\mathrm{k}$ is any positive integer",
              "isCorrect": false,
              "image": null
            }
          ],
          "correctValue": null,
          "solution": {
            "text": "We have, $\\sin ^{4} x-(k+2) \\sin ^{2} x-(k+3)=0$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin ^{2} x=\\frac{(k+2) \\pm \\sqrt{(k+2)^{2}+4(k+3)}}{2}$\r\n\r\n$=\\frac{(k+2) \\pm(k+4)}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin ^{2} x=k+3\\left(\\because \\sin ^{2} x=-1\\right.$ is not possible)\r\n\r\nSince $0 \\leq \\sin ^{2} x \\leq 1$\r\n\r\n$\\therefore 0 \\leq \\mathrm{k}+3 \\leq 1$ or $-3 \\leq \\mathrm{k} \\leq-2$",
            "image": null
          },
